        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8745-1",
        "name": "USN-8745-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that KissFFT incorrectly handled certain large Fourier transform sizes on 32-bit architectures. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause KissFFT to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-34297)  It was discovered that KissFFT incorrectly handled certain multidimensional Fourier transform sizes. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause KissFFT to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-41445)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2025-34297",
          "CVE-2026-41445"
        ]
      },
